 "fps": 24,
 "duration": 27.87,
 "lines": "She watches us / gather my things to go. / before I go— / I call on my Father / summon his calming / demeanor / from the yonders / & we walk for years / & travel east toward the sunrises / & retrace his footsteps / now & then. / guiding a settling down / moon—the way / it used to leave / & my tears fall between / the creases in wave / shadows / of the inner harbor—",
 "read": "She watches us gather my things to go. Before I go, I call on my father. Summon his calming demeanor from the yonders and we walk for years and travel east toward the sunrises and retrace his footsteps now and then. Guiding a settling down moon the way it used to leave and my tears fall between the creases and wave shadows of the inner harbor.",
